// SIR outbreak among 9 susceptibles exposed to one chronic carrier, in
// classic PEPA. Infection is cooperation on `infect`: susceptibles offer
// it actively at `beta`, the carrier passively (`infty`), so the
// susceptibles set the pace. Recovery interleaves on its own (note it is
// *not* in the cooperation set: cooperating on it would block it, since
// only SI performs it).
//
// Classic PEPA needs static roles: one array cannot mix active and
// passive offers of one action (its apparent rate would be undefined),
// so susceptibles become `SI` — which offers no `infect` — instead of a
// shared `I`. The total pressure scales with susceptibles only
// (#S * beta). For true mass action (#S * beta * #I), where individuals
// change roles freely, see sir_fun.pepa (functional rates) and sir.prism.
// Rates are per day.

beta  = 0.3;   // infection attempts per susceptible per day
gamma = 0.1;   // recovery rate per infected per day

S = (infect, beta).SI;
SI = (recover, gamma).R;
R = 0;
Carrier = (infect, infty).Carrier;

S[9] <infect> Carrier
